{
  "answer": "To configure CORS to allow requests from specific origins in FastAPI, you can use the `CORSMiddleware` and specify the `allow_origins` parameter. Here is an example of how to do this:\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n# Define allowed origins\nallowed_origins = ['https://example.com', 'https://www.example.com']\n\n# Configure CORSMiddleware\napp.add_middleware(\n    CORSMiddleware,\n    allow_origins=allowed_origins,\n    allow_credentials=True,\n    allow_methods=['GET', 'POST'],\n    allow_headers=['Content-Type', 'Access-Control-Allow-Credentials']\n)\n```\n\nThis configuration is supported by [tutorial/cors-5].",
